{
  "manufacturer": "Laars",
  "manufacturer_slug": "laars",
  "model": "OmniTherm - ProtoNode",
  "model_slug": "omnitherm-protonode",
  "aliases": [
    "OmniTherm",
    "Laars OmniTherm",
    "ProtoNode FPC-N34",
    "ProtoNode FPC-N35",
    "FPC-N34-0701",
    "Laars ProtoNode"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller gateway",
  "applies_to": "Laars OmniTherm units, read through a ProtoNode FPC-N34 gateway.",
  "summary": "The ProtoNode reads the OmniTherm control over Modbus RTU and serves 121 objects per unit. Analog inputs cover temperatures, flame signal, 0-10 V inputs and outputs, firing rate, lockout and alarm codes, burner status, history counters and cascade lead/lag states; binary inputs break out the safety chain and output bits. Writable AVs and BVs hold the CH1, CH2, DHW and cascade enables, set points and PID terms plus three demand switches.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "50000 + device Node-ID",
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Each unit on the ProtoNode's RS-485 bus shows up as its own BACnet device, and every one uses the same object IDs. The device instance is Node_Offset (default 50000) plus the unit's Node-ID, so Node-ID 1 = device 50001.",
    "The mapping has no read/write column. AV, BV and MV objects are mapped to Metasys N2 outputs and LonWorks input variables, so they are listed here as writable; AI, BI and MI objects are read-only.",
    "The mapping gives no units for temperatures or set points.",
    "Bit-mapped registers (safety chain, non-safety chain, digital outputs, gas and pilot valve) are split into one BI per bit; the object names here join the register name and the bit label.",
    "Compared with the MagnaTherm list this one has no DHW recirculation objects but adds the auxiliary 1 output (AI 26) and fan 1 speed (AI 27)."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Enable CH1 with AV 0, set BV 1 CH 1 Demand switch for a call for heat and write the CH1 set point (or the cascade CH set point for a cascade). Read the run contact, Burner Status 2, outlet temperature and firing rate, and watch the alarm contact and lockout code.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "name": "CH1 Enable/Disable",
        "why": "CH1 enable (1 = enable)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "CH 1 Demand switch",
        "why": "CH1 call for heat (1 = heat demand)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "CH1 Set Point",
        "why": "CH1 water set point"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 27",
        "name": "Cascade CH Set Point",
        "why": "Set point when units run in cascade"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 11",
        "name": "Digital Output Status - Run contact",
        "why": "Run output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 85",
        "name": "Burner Status 2",
        "why": "Burner state; 51 = firing, 1 = locked out"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Outlet sensor",
        "why": "Outlet water temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 33",
        "name": "Modulating Burner1 Firing rate",
        "why": "Burner 1 firing rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 12",
        "name": "Digital Output Status - Alarm Contact",
        "why": "Alarm output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "Lockout code",
        "why": "Lockout code (0-29)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "AV 0 CH1 Enable/Disable (0 = disable, 1 = enable) and BV 1 CH 1 Demand switch (0 = no heat demand, 1 = heat demand). CH2 and DHW have matching objects.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device instance = Node_Offset + unit Node-ID. Node_Offset defaults to 50000 and is changed in the ProtoNode web configurator; Node-IDs must be unique, 1-255.",
      "Unit to ProtoNode: Modbus RTU, 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.",
      "Default ProtoNode IP address 192.168.1.24, mask 255.255.255.0. Choose BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP with the Protocol Selector, then add one profile per device with its Node-ID.",
      "With more than one device on a ProtoNode, set BACnet Virtual Server Nodes to Yes. For BACnet MS/TP also set MAC address, baud rate and Max Master.",
      "Two or more ProtoNodes on the same subnet need different BACnet Network Numbers (default 50).",
      "A ProtoNode handles 1,500 registers in total; this profile uses 174 per device."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "AI 36 Alarm reason uses codes 30-44, continuing the lockout code list in AI 35.",
      "PID terms for each circuit are writable AVs; they are tuning values, not BMS commands."
    ]
  },
